  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "NL80211 + IEEE 802.11: Dissect Beacon IEs containing TAG_SSID correctly",
  "description": "IEEE 802.11 assigns tag 0 to TAG_SSID, which creates some confusion\nbetween zero-padding at the end of a collection of tags and that\ntag. There is a workaround in the IEEE 802.11 dissector for that\ninvolving a global variable in ieee_80211_add_tagged_parameters.\nThis is necessary for Beacon frames (and anything else that may\nhave that tag.)\n\nExpose ieee_80211_add_tagged_parameters() in the header so that\nthe netlink-nl80211 dissector can call it to dissect a series\nof tags, since some of the IEs in nl80211 are beacon frames. Without\nthis, those tags are incorrectly treated as padding.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
